**=================================================================================================
** Winkler L-shaped panel -- shared model, included by the three WinklerL_*.inp variants.
**
** Units: mm, N, MPa (N/mm^2).
**
** Geometry (x right, y up, z through the thickness of 50 mm):
**   concrete L-panel     x 0..500, y 100..500, without the cut-out x > 250, y < 250
**   steel support block  x 0..250, y 0..100, under the left leg
**   steel load block     x 400..500, y 250..350, at the underside of the right arm
** Mesh: mesh.inp holds 20-node hexahedra (GC3D20R concrete: displacement + nonlocal damage; C3D20R steel:
** displacement only), generated from the linear mesh_hex8.inp by hex8_to_hex20.py -- h-adaptivity
** refines HEX20-family elements only.
**
** Boundary conditions (the same in every variant, see the *step in each file):
**   setBottom  bottom face of the support block, clamped (u_x = u_y = u_z = 0)
**   setBack    the complete back face z = 0, supported in z (u_z = 0, a symmetry condition): it holds
**              the plate against out-of-plane bending
**   setLoad    the load line in the load block, displaced upwards (u_y) -- the loading
**
** Concrete: gradient-enhanced concrete damage plasticity (Marmot GCDP, a private Marmot module),
** Winkler's E, nu and tensile strength ftu = 2.70 MPa.
**=================================================================================================
*include, input=mesh.inp

*material, name=GCDP, id=GCDP
** Parameter order and names as read by Marmot's GCDP (19 values):
**   E, nu            elasticity
**   fcy, fcu         uniaxial compressive yield and ultimate strength
**   fbu              biaxial compressive ultimate strength
**   ftu              uniaxial tensile strength
**   Df, Ah..Dh       plasticity parameters (Df dilatancy, Ah..Dh hardening and ductility)
**   As, epsF         damage (softening) parameters
**   lDamage          nonlocal radius of the damage field [mm]
**   m                nonlocal weighting parameter
**   maxDmg           damage cap -- damage never exceeds it
**   drvtvMthd        derivative method of the return mapping (0 automatic, 1 central differences)
**   dTThrshHold      below this time increment the damaged elastic stiffness is used (0: never)
**   viscosity        Duvaut-Lions viscoplasticity (0: rate independent)
**E         nu          fcy         fcu         fbu         ftu         Df          Ah
25850.0,    0.18,       10.33,      31.0,       35.96,      2.70,       0.85,       0.08,
**Bh        Ch          Dh          As          epsF        lDamage     m           maxDmg
0.003,      2.0,        0.000001,   15,         0.0017,     2,          1.0,        0.99,
**drvtvMthd dTThrshHold viscosity
0,          0,          0

*material, name=linearElastic, id=steelLoad
** E, nu
37000.0, 0.3
*material, name=linearElastic, id=steelBottom
44400.0, 0.3

*section, name=secConc, material=GCDP, type=solid
secConc
*section, name=secSteelLoad, material=steelLoad, type=solid
secSteelLoad
*section, name=secSteelBottom, material=steelBottom, type=solid
secSteelBottom

*fieldOutput
>>perNode, elSet=all, name=displacement, field=displacement, result=U
>>perNode, elSet=secConc, name=nonlocalDamage, field=nonlocal damage, result=U
** per element: the largest value over its 8 quadrature points
>>perElement, elSet=secConc, name=damage, result=omega, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='np.max(x,axis=1)'
** largest plastic hardening variable of each element -- what the h-adaptivity marker of variant 3 thresholds
>>perElement, elSet=secConc, name=alphaP, result=alphaP, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='np.max(x,axis=1)'
